{"id":"17L","title":"Selfishness","part":{"n":17,"title":"Personal character traits"},"url":"/law/17-personal-character-traits/17l","entries":[{"id":"17L.1","text":"He that wishes one well but does not give to him what he needs exhibits selfishness.","refs":[{"book":"James","chapter":2,"verses":"15-16"},{"book":"1 John","chapter":3,"verses":"17"}],"citation":"James 2:15-16; 1 John 3:17."},{"id":"17L.2","text":"We should not desire to please ourselves.","refs":[{"book":"Romans","chapter":15,"verses":"1"},{"book":"2 Timothy","chapter":3,"verses":"2"}],"citation":"Rom. 15:1; 2 Tim. 3:2."},{"id":"17L.3","text":"A servant of God is to act for the benefit or profit of others.","refs":[{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":56,"verses":"11"},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":10,"verses":"33"}],"citation":"Isa. 56:11; 1 Cor. 10:33."},{"id":"17L.4","text":"Selfishness is inconsistent with the communion of Christians.","refs":[{"book":"Romans","chapter":12,"verses":"4-4"},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":12,"verses":"12-27"}],"citation":"Rom. 12:4-4; 1 Cor. 12:12-27."},{"id":"17L.5","text":"Let us not please ourselves, but let every one of us please his neighbor.","refs":[{"book":"Romans","chapter":15,"verses":"1-3"}],"citation":"Rom. 15:1-3."},{"id":"17L.6","text":"No one should merely seek or look out for his own interest, but also for the interests of others.","refs":[{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":10,"verses":"24"},{"book":"Philippians","chapter":2,"verses":"4"}],"citation":"1 Cor. 10:24; Phil. 2:4."},{"id":"17L.7","text":"The selfish shall receive punishment according to their ways.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":21,"verses":"13"}],"citation":"Prov. 21:13."}]}